      "message": "fix(app): a typed Slot's caps no longer read as a gouge\n\nThe stadium a Slot is verified against drew each round end as 16 chords\ninscribed in the true arc, up to h(1 - cos 5.625 deg) inside it: for a\n6 mm cutter on a 6 mm slot the cap-centre position read 2.9855 mm from\nthe boundary against the gouge law's r - tol = 2.99, so every plunge and\nfeed of a slot whose cutter reaches its end was a Gouge and never posted.\n\nThe caps are now the polygon circumscribed about the arc (tangent\nchords, corners at h / cos(phi/2)), with the chord count chosen so a\ncorner stands at most 1 um outside the arc. A tangent cutter verifies\nclean; a 0.05 mm over-cut of the cap still convicts. GOUGE_TOL is\nunchanged and the posted G-code does not change.\n\nFixes #510\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
